<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Ruby series</th>
      {%- for base_image in base_images %}
        <th>{{ base_image }}</th>
      {%- endfor %}
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {%- for row in rows %}
      <tr{% if row.style %} style="{{ row.style }}"{% endif %}>
        <td>{{ row.major_minor }}{{ row.label }}</td>
        {%- for version in row.versions %}
          <td>{{ version or "-" }}</td>
        {%- endfor %}
      </tr>
    {%- endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>

To use a Ruby version, specify it in your `Gemfile`. For example:

```ruby
# Gemfile
ruby '{{ example }}'
```

Then, with that Ruby version installed locally, update your `Gemfile.lock` by running:

```term
$ bundle update --ruby
```
